+# The Daily Grind
+
+Node 24+ homepage with browser-assisted email ownership verification. Install with `pnpm install` and deploy with `pnpm start`. `pnpm build` performs syntax checks without opening a listener.
+
+## Deployment
+
+- Set `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin (for example `https://coffee.example.com`). It is the trusted audience and CSRF origin; do not infer it from forwarded headers.
+- Register that origin for the [Chrome Email Verification origin trial](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification) and set `ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN`. HTTPS, browser participation, a participating provider, and an active provider session are required. No public token can be supplied before the deployment origin is known.
+- `PORT` defaults to 11222. Terminate HTTPS at the deployment proxy. Production HTTPS origins receive Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax session cookies.
+- Set `DATABASE_PATH` to a persistent writable SQLite file. The default is `rewards.sqlite`. Back it up and restrict filesystem access; it contains customer names/emails. This implementation is intended for one Node deployment with persistent storage. Add ingress rate limiting before public rollout.
+
+The form must be served by `server.mjs`, not a static file host. The server renders a fresh 256-bit challenge nonce into the native form, stores it in SQLite behind an opaque session cookie, and serves HTML with `Cache-Control: no-store`. POST `/api/verify-email` atomically consumes that challenge even on failed attempts. Every response renders a fresh challenge for retries.
+
+Verification uses `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose`: email matching (case insensitive), DNS issuer delegation, issuer discovery, public JWKS, asymmetric issuer signature, expiration/freshness, holder signature, audience, nonce, and `sd_hash`. Provider fetches use public IPv4 addresses pinned to the TLS connection, bounded responses, a timeout, and no redirects. Tokens are never logged or persisted. Verified members are persisted with unique lowercase emails; duplicates do not produce a second membership. This enrollment does not establish an authenticated login session.
+
+There is deliberately no OTP/magic-link fallback. Empty, expired, invalid or unavailable proofs return an actionable message and do not create accounts or send mail. Browser support cannot be reliably feature-detected. Do not simulate proof in client JavaScript or intercept form submission: the browser populates the hidden input during native submission.
+
+The pre-existing menu, ordering, location, privacy and company links require their own destination pages; those pages were not part of this homepage. Rewards terms are available inline. Photos are hosted by Unsplash; fonts by Google Fonts.
